    {
      "issue": "The home config's `watch` value is silently dropped whenever review.mjs loads a different config file that lacks the key. loadConfig returns the first existing file whole: REVIEW_CONFIG (`if (!repo) return config`, line 363) or an untracked repo `.claude/review-config.json` (withoutRepoCommands returns it unchanged when repoFileIsOwn, line 232). Only `merge` and `security` are back-filled from home (lines 366-367); `watch` is carried over only on the tracked-file path (`fromHome`, line 236). So with home `watch: off` (or `pane`) and such a file present, WATCH falls to the built-in `sidebar`. This contradicts the README ('a home-config setting only') and the ACS Settings row, and diverges from ask-model.mjs:188-197, which reads the home files only: on the same machine a review shows sidebar lines while ask-model honours off/pane.",
      "file": "packs/review-gate/runtime/review.mjs",
      "line": "395",
      "quote": "  const mode = String(cfg('REVIEW_WATCH', 'watch', 'sidebar')).trim().toLowerCase()",
      "suggestion": "Resolve watch as env > loaded config's own `watch` (already stripped when tracked) > homeKey(homes, 'watch') > 'sidebar', e.g. back-fill `checked.watch`/`config.watch` from homeKey in loadConfig the way merge and security are, including the REVIEW_CONFIG path.",
      "likelihood": 2,
      "impact": 3,
      "protected": false,
      "trigger": "Home config has `watch: off` or `pane` (set in ACS), and the review runs in a repo with an untracked `.claude/review-config.json` that has no `watch` key (e.g. one holding only verifyCmd), or with REVIEW_CONFIG pointing at a file without `watch`. The review then shows sidebar lines (or no pane) against the saved setting.",
      "preExisting": false,
      "risk": 6,
      "severity": "low",
      "filed": true,
      "status": "verified-quote",
      "id": "f1"
    },
    {
      "issue": "The slice suffix can never appear for a `--slices` run. Slice children carry REVIEW_WATCH_CHILD=1, so startWatch returns (review.mjs:5027) before writing a run file; the ancestor walk `run ||= runs.get(q)` (line 941) therefore only ever finds the parent's run file, and the `--slices` parent has SLICE null (its groups go to children via REVIEW_PATHS). Every slice's reviewer and security call gets the same prefix, so up to 4 parallel slices (8 lines) are indistinguishable in the sidebar and pane. `run.slice` only shows for a single top-level REVIEW_PATHS run. Cosmetic: nothing else is affected.",
      "file": "lib/agent.js",
      "line": "947",
      "quote": "        const slice = run.slice !== undefined && run.slice !== null ? ` · ${shown(run.slice, 24)}` : '';",
      "suggestion": "Give the watcher the slice per child without a second watcher: either have a REVIEW_WATCH_CHILD run still write its run file (pid, kind, slice) and skip only the probe and spawn, or have the parent record each slice child's pid and group in its own run file, so the ancestor walk at line 941 finds it.",
      "likelihood": 5,
      "impact": 1,
